{
  "id": "python_py_fastapi_response_openapi",
  "title": "Response models and OpenAPI",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "testId": "python_test_py_fastapi_response_openapi_en",
  "estimatedMinutes": 17,
  "sources": [
    "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/response-model/",
    "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/metadata/"
  ],
  "spans": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHY USE THIS?\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI builds JSON APIs that web and mobile applications call over HTTP; type annotations help validate inputs and describe the API contract.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PURPOSE AND REAL-WORLD USE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#6A1B9A",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "response_model",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " defines which fields the API returns, validates the result, and adds it to OpenAPI. This helps prevent accidental data exposure and gives clients a stable contract.\n\n",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "To run these examples locally, install ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "pip install fastapi uvicorn httpx",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " plus any extra package named in the lesson. Save the server example as ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app.py",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and start ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "uvicorn app:app --reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ". ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "--reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is for development only.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHERE DOES THIS APPEAR IN REAL LIFE?\nA user record stores ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "password_hash",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", but the response model exposes only ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "id",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "name",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ".\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If this part is omitted: Without a response model, extra internal fields can leak and docs may be vague; make the return contract explicit.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMPLETE RUNNABLE EXAMPLE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nclass UserPublic(BaseModel):\n    id: int\n    name: str\n\n@app.get(\"/users/{user_id}\", response_model=UserPublic)\nasync def read_user(user_id: int):\n    return {\"id\": user_id, \"name\": \"Ada\", \"password_hash\": \"never-return-this\"}\n",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "REQUEST AND EXPECTED RESPONSE\n",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "Request: GET /users/1\nResponse: 200 OK; public fields only: {\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Ada\"}",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE CODE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi import FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports FastAPI so the program can create its application object; without it, ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is undefined.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from pydantic import BaseModel",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports a required type or tool; without it, the name is unavailable.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app = FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " creates the ASGI application that holds the routes and is passed to the server.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "class UserPublic(BaseModel):",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines a Pydantic data model; its field types form the request-body contract.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "id: int",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Declares an expected model field and type; omitting it changes the body contract.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "name: str",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Declares an expected model field and type; omitting it changes the body contract.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "@app.get(\"/users/{user_id}\", response_model=UserPublic)",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds an HTTP method and URL path to this function; without the decorator, it is not an API endpoint.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "async def read_user(user_id: int):",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines the endpoint the server calls; parameter names help bind path, query, or body data.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "return {\"id\": user_id, \"name\": \"Ada\", \"password_hash\": \"never-return-this\"}",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Returns the HTTP response value; FastAPI converts it to JSON and applies the response model.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PRACTICE: CHECK IT WITH AN HTTP CLIENT\n",
      "size": 19,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This complete file calls the app locally with TestClient; it does not open a server port. Install ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "httpx",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " for TestClient.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMPLETE RUNNABLE CLIENT TEST\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nclass UserPublic(BaseModel):\n    id: int\n    name: str\n\n@app.get(\"/users/{user_id}\", response_model=UserPublic)\nasync def read_user(user_id: int):\n    return {\"id\": user_id, \"name\": \"Ada\", \"password_hash\": \"never-return-this\"}\n\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\n\nwith TestClient(app) as client:\n    response = client.get(\"/users/1\")\n    print(response.status_code, response.json())\n",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXPECTED CLIENT-TEST OUTPUT\n",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "200 {'id': 1, 'name': 'Ada'}",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE CODE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi import FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports FastAPI so the program can create its application object; without it, ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is undefined.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from pydantic import BaseModel",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports a required type or tool; without it, the name is unavailable.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app = FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " creates the ASGI application that holds the routes and is passed to the server.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "class UserPublic(BaseModel):",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines a Pydantic data model; its field types form the request-body contract.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "id: int",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Declares an expected model field and type; omitting it changes the body contract.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "name: str",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Declares an expected model field and type; omitting it changes the body contract.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "@app.get(\"/users/{user_id}\", response_model=UserPublic)",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds an HTTP method and URL path to this function; without the decorator, it is not an API endpoint.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "async def read_user(user_id: int):",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines the endpoint the server calls; parameter names help bind path, query, or body data.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "return {\"id\": user_id, \"name\": \"Ada\", \"password_hash\": \"never-return-this\"}",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Returns the HTTP response value; FastAPI converts it to JSON and applies the response model.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi.testclient import TestClient",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports TestClient so an HTTP request can exercise the app without opening a server port.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "with TestClient(app) as client:",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Creates a test HTTP client for the app and closes it when the context ends.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "response = client.get(\"/users/1\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Sends the stated GET request through the test client and stores the response.\n",
