      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "print(response.status_code, response.json())",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Reads and prints both the HTTP status code and parsed JSON response.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMMON MISTAKES\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#C62828",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Returning a database object directly and assuming every field is public; define a separate response model.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "title": "Practical tip",
      "text": "Inspect `/openapi.json`, then test that an `internal_note` field absent from the model is not exposed."
    },
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "title": "One level deeper",
      "text": "OpenAPI is a machine-readable contract from which `/docs` is generated. Documentation does not provide authentication or authorization."
    },
    {
      "type": "warning",
      "title": "Important warning",
      "text": "Use response models to exclude sensitive fields; a field missing from docs is not proof that the server hides it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUICK RECALL\n",
      "size": 20,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Question: Which action best prevents the common mistake from this lesson?\n",
